# Five people, ten identities. Everyone here has committed under at least two,
# because the GitHub web editor uses a noreply address while a local clone uses
# whatever `git config user.email` says - and two of us also changed our display
# name partway through.
#
# Without this, `git shortlog -sn`, `git blame` and GitHub's contributor graph
# count the same person twice. Elyesa's 115 commits show as 80 and 35; Athith's
# 110 show as 94 and 16. Anyone judging the repository by its insights tab sees
# a team that did roughly a third less work than it did.
#
# Left of the angle brackets is the name to show; the entries after it are the
# identities to fold into it. Check with: git shortlog -sne --all

